libv4l-rkmpp: accept VIDIOC_S_CTRL, and stop padding the encoded size

Two independent defects, both of which stop ustreamer from using this
plugin as a hardware MJPEG encoder. Measured on an OrangePi RK3399 with
the MPP VEPU2 enabled (kernel patch 0013).

1. VIDIOC_S_CTRL returns ENOTTY.

   Every control the encoder supports is already implemented - bitrate,
   the H.264 profile/level/QP set, header mode, the lot - but only under
   VIDIOC_S_EXT_CTRLS. The older single-control ioctl falls through to
   the default case and returns ENOTTY.

   That is not a cosmetic gap. ustreamer's V4L2 M2M encoder sets its
   controls *before* it touches a format, and treats a failed S_CTRL as
   fatal, so it aborts on the first one and never reaches the code that
   works. For --encoder=m2m-video the whole difference between "unusable"
   and "working" is one control, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_BITRATE, which this
   plugin has handled all along.

   Wrap the v4l2_control into a one-element v4l2_ext_controls and forward
   it. The class is derived from the ID, so a control outside the MPEG
   class still fails, in exactly the place it failed before.

2. The encoder is told the macroblock-aligned size.

   rkmpp_try_fmt() rounds width and height up to whole macroblocks in the
   caller's struct, and rkmpp_s_fmt() then stores that rounded size as the
   queue format. rkmpp_enc_apply_prep_cfg() reads it back and hands it to
   MPP as prep:width/prep:height, so 1920x1080 is encoded, and marked in
   the bitstream, as 1920x1088 - eight rows of padding presented as
   picture. MPP itself gets this right: mpi_enc_test on the same hardware
   produces a correctly-sized 1920x1080 stream.

   The rounded size is the right thing for sizing buffers and must stay in
   queue->format. Record the requested size alongside it and use that for
   the encoder configuration.

   try_fmt both rounds up and clamps to the hardware limits. A clamp has
   to stand - it is the hardware talking - so the requested size is only
   honoured when it lies within one macroblock below the value that came
   back, which is the signature of rounding rather than clamping.

3. A compressed format with sizeimage == 0 is rejected.

   V4L2 has the driver fill sizeimage in; requiring the application to
   supply it turns a legal request into EINVAL. ustreamer sets it only on
   the H.264 path - for MJPEG it leaves the field at zero and expects a
   default - so with (1) and (2) fixed this is still the last thing
   between it and the hardware encoder.

   Default to one byte per macroblock-padded pixel, with a floor for the
   small sizes where a JPEG's headers outweigh its data. A 1080p JPEG of
   pure noise at quality 80, far worse than any screen, measured under
   half of that.

4. Importing a DMABUF always asks for write access.

   rkmpp_copy_buffer() maps the caller's dma-buf PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE
   whichever way it is about to copy. VIDIOC_EXPBUF with flags == 0
   hands back a read-only dma-buf - videobuf2 passes flags & O_ACCMODE
   through and O_RDONLY is zero - so importing a capture buffer fails,
   and ustreamer exports exactly that way. Map read-only when the copy
   only reads.

5. The JPEG encoder is unreachable through its own API.

   V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG is not in the encoder's format table, so an
   application asking for one still image per buffer gets EINVAL and has
   to pretend it wants a video stream. And rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls()
   already handles V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY, but rejects
   anything outside the MPEG control class first - so a control that was
   implemented all along could never be set. Add the fourcc, and let the
   JPEG class through.

6. MJPEG quality is left to a rate controller.

   Only jpeg:q_factor was set, leaving qf_min/qf_max at 1/99 and CBR in
   charge, so the quality factor moves frame to frame. Constant quality
   is what MJPEG is for, and a hunting quality factor also means
   identical input encodes to different bytes, which silently breaks any
   consumer that drops duplicate frames by comparing them. With a static
   screen, ustreamer's --drop-same-frames went from ~1 fps on the wire
   to 12. Pin qf_min and qf_max to the requested factor.

The existing VIDIOC_S_SELECTION path already overrides (2), so anything
that sets a crop explicitly is unaffected.

diff --git a/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h b/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h
index 722a81a..f71e2c3 100644
--- a/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h
+++ b/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h
@@ -110,6 +110,10 @@ extern int rkmpp_log_level;
 #define MPP_VIDEO_CodingNone	MPP_VIDEO_CodingUnused
 
 #define RKMPP_MB_DIM		16
+
+/* Floor for a defaulted compressed sizeimage; a JPEG's headers alone are
+ * larger than width*height once the picture gets small enough. */
+#define RKMPP_MIN_COMPRESSED_SIZE	(128 * 1024)
 #define RKMPP_SB_DIM		64
 
 #define RKMPP_MAX_PLANES	3
@@ -236,6 +240,15 @@ struct rkmpp_buf_queue {
 
 	const struct rkmpp_fmt *rkmpp_format;
 	struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane format;
+
+	/*
+	 * The size requested by S_FMT, before try_fmt rounded it up to whole
+	 * macroblocks. "format" carries the rounded size because that is what
+	 * sizes the buffers; the encoder has to be told the real one, or a
+	 * 1080-line frame is encoded, and marked in the bitstream, as 1088.
+	 */
+	uint32_t visible_width;
+	uint32_t visible_height;
 };
 
 /**
diff --git a/src/libv4l-rkmpp-enc.c b/src/libv4l-rkmpp-enc.c
index 2839119..5b6aaae 100644
--- a/src/libv4l-rkmpp-enc.c
+++ b/src/libv4l-rkmpp-enc.c
@@ -113,6 +113,29 @@ static struct rkmpp_fmt rkmpp_enc_fmts[] = {
 			.max_height = 1088,
 			.step_height = RKMPP_MB_DIM,
 		}
+	},
+	/*
+	 * The same encoder under the fourcc that V4L2 defines for a single
+	 * still image. MJPEG is a sequence of these, and MPP is handed the
+	 * identical coding type either way, but an application asking for
+	 * one JPEG per buffer is entitled to say so - ustreamer's m2m-image
+	 * encoder does, and was refused. Note "JPEG" is a substring of
+	 * "MJPEG", so a device configured with codecs=MJPEG exposes both.
+	 */
+	{
+		.name = "JPEG",
+		.fourcc = V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG,
+		.num_planes = 1,
+		.type = MPP_VIDEO_CodingMJPEG,
+		.format = MPP_FMT_BUTT,
+		.frmsize = {
+			.min_width = 96,
+			.max_width = 1920,
+			.step_width = RKMPP_MB_DIM,
+			.min_height = 96,
+			.max_height = 1088,
+			.step_height = RKMPP_MB_DIM,
+		}
 	}
 };
 
@@ -531,7 +554,23 @@ static int rkmpp_enc_apply_mjpeg_cfg(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "jpeg:q_factor", enc->mjpeg.quality ? enc->mjpeg.quality : 80);
+	/*
+	 * Pin the quality factor instead of leaving the rate controller a
+	 * range to hunt within. Two reasons. Constant quality is what MJPEG
+	 * is for - a screen that is not changing should cost nothing, not a
+	 * steady bitrate. And with a range, identical input encodes to
+	 * different bytes every frame, which silently defeats any consumer
+	 * that drops duplicate frames by comparing them: ustreamer's
+	 * --drop-same-frames went from dropping ~59 of 60 to almost none,
+	 * and an idle screen went from 1 fps on the wire to 12.
+	 */
+	{
+		const int qf = enc->mjpeg.quality ? enc->mjpeg.quality : 80;
+
+		mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "jpeg:q_factor", qf);
+		mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "jpeg:qf_min", qf);
+		mpp_enc_cfg_set_s32(cfg, "jpeg:qf_max", qf);
+	}
 
 	ret = ctx->mpi->control(ctx->mpp, MPP_ENC_SET_CFG, cfg);
 	if (ret != MPP_OK) {
@@ -565,8 +604,12 @@ static int rkmpp_enc_apply_input_cfg(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	enc->width = enc->crop.width ? enc->crop.width : fmt->width;
-	enc->height = enc->crop.height ? enc->crop.height : fmt->height;
+	enc->width = enc->crop.width ? enc->crop.width :
+		(ctx->output.visible_width ?
+		 ctx->output.visible_width : fmt->width);
+	enc->height = enc->crop.height ? enc->crop.height :
+		(ctx->output.visible_height ?
+		 ctx->output.visible_height : fmt->height);
 	enc->hstride = fmt->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline;
 	enc->vstride = fmt->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage /
 		fmt->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline;
@@ -720,6 +763,7 @@ static int rkmpp_enc_streamon(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc,
 		enc->type = VP8;
 		break;
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG:
+	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG:
 		enc->type = MJPEG;
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -994,8 +1038,14 @@ static int rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc,
 
 	ENTER();
 
+	/*
+	 * V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY is handled below but lives in the
+	 * JPEG class, so this check made it unreachable: a control that was
+	 * implemented all along could never be set.
+	 */
 	if (ext_ctrls->ctrl_class != V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG &&
-	    ext_ctrls->ctrl_class != V4L2_CID_MPEG_CLASS)
+	    ext_ctrls->ctrl_class != V4L2_CID_MPEG_CLASS &&
+	    ext_ctrls->ctrl_class != V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_JPEG)
 		RETURN_ERR(EINVAL, -1);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ext_ctrls->count; i++) {
@@ -1224,6 +1274,22 @@ static int rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int rkmpp_enc_s_ctrl(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc,
+			    struct v4l2_control *ctrl)
+{
+	struct v4l2_ext_control ext_ctrl = {
+		.id = ctrl->id,
+		.value = ctrl->value,
+	};
+	struct v4l2_ext_controls ext_ctrls = {
+		.ctrl_class = V4L2_CTRL_ID2CLASS(ctrl->id),
+		.count = 1,
+		.controls = &ext_ctrl,
+	};
+
+	return rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls(enc, &ext_ctrls);
+}
+
 static int rkmpp_enc_cmd(struct rkmpp_enc_context *enc,
 			 struct v4l2_encoder_cmd *cmd)
 {
@@ -1379,6 +1445,19 @@ int rkmpp_enc_ioctl(void *data, unsigned long cmd, void *arg)
 	case VIDIOC_S_EXT_CTRLS:
 		ret = rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls(enc, arg);
 		break;
+	case VIDIOC_S_CTRL:
+		/*
+		 * Every control this plugin understands is already implemented,
+		 * but only behind S_EXT_CTRLS. Applications that use the older
+		 * single-control ioctl - ustreamer among them - got ENOTTY from
+		 * the default case and gave up before touching a format, which
+		 * made the encoder look unusable when only the doorbell was
+		 * missing. Wrap and forward; the class comes from the ID, so an
+		 * out-of-class control still fails in one place, inside
+		 * rkmpp_enc_s_ext_ctrls().
+		 */
+		ret = rkmpp_enc_s_ctrl(enc, arg);
+		break;
 	case VIDIOC_ENCODER_CMD:
 		ret = rkmpp_enc_cmd(enc, arg);
 		break;
diff --git a/src/libv4l-rkmpp.c b/src/libv4l-rkmpp.c
index 53b743f..b4ab694 100644
--- a/src/libv4l-rkmpp.c
+++ b/src/libv4l-rkmpp.c
@@ -335,8 +335,27 @@ int rkmpp_try_fmt(struct rkmpp_context *ctx, struct v4l2_format *f)
 
 	if (compressed) {
 		if (pix_fmt_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage == 0) {
-			LOGE("sizeimage of compressed format must be given\n");
-			RETURN_ERR(EINVAL, -1);
+			/*
+			 * V4L2 has the driver fill sizeimage in, not the
+			 * application; requiring it here rejects callers that
+			 * are doing nothing wrong. ustreamer sets it only for
+			 * H.264 - for MJPEG it leaves the field at zero and
+			 * expects a default - so this refusal is the whole
+			 * reason it cannot use the MJPEG encoder.
+			 *
+			 * One byte per padded pixel. A 1080p JPEG of pure
+			 * noise at quality 80, which is far worse than any
+			 * screen, measured under half of that.
+			 */
+			uint32_t size =
+				round_up(pix_fmt_mp->width, RKMPP_MB_DIM) *
+				round_up(pix_fmt_mp->height, RKMPP_MB_DIM);
+
+			if (size < RKMPP_MIN_COMPRESSED_SIZE)
+				size = RKMPP_MIN_COMPRESSED_SIZE;
+
+			pix_fmt_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = size;
+			LOGV(1, "defaulted compressed sizeimage to %d\n", size);
 		}
 
 		pix_fmt_mp->num_planes = fmt->num_planes;
@@ -399,11 +418,15 @@ int rkmpp_try_fmt(struct rkmpp_context *ctx, struct v4l2_format *f)
 int rkmpp_s_fmt(struct rkmpp_context *ctx, struct v4l2_format *f)
 {
 	struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *pix_fmt_mp = &f->fmt.pix_mp;
+	uint32_t req_width, req_height;
 	struct rkmpp_buf_queue *queue;
 	int ret;
 
 	ENTER();
 
+	req_width = pix_fmt_mp->width;
+	req_height = pix_fmt_mp->height;
+
 	queue = rkmpp_get_queue(ctx, f->type);
 	if (!queue)
 		RETURN_ERR(errno, -1);
@@ -430,6 +453,21 @@ int rkmpp_s_fmt(struct rkmpp_context *ctx, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		rkmpp_find_fmt(ctx, pix_fmt_mp->pixelformat);
 	queue->format = *pix_fmt_mp;
 
+	/*
+	 * Undo the macroblock rounding, and only that. try_fmt both rounds up
+	 * and clamps to the hardware's limits; a clamp must stand, so accept
+	 * the requested size only when it sits within one macroblock below
+	 * what came back.
+	 */
+	queue->visible_width = pix_fmt_mp->width;
+	queue->visible_height = pix_fmt_mp->height;
+	if (req_width && req_width <= pix_fmt_mp->width &&
+	    pix_fmt_mp->width - req_width < RKMPP_MB_DIM)
+		queue->visible_width = req_width;
+	if (req_height && req_height <= pix_fmt_mp->height &&
+	    pix_fmt_mp->height - req_height < RKMPP_MB_DIM)
+		queue->visible_height = req_height;
+
 	LEAVE();
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/src/utils.c b/src/utils.c
index 1274339..b88a276 100644
--- a/src/utils.c
+++ b/src/utils.c
@@ -54,8 +54,22 @@ static int rkmpp_copy_buffer(struct rkmpp_context *ctx,
 
 		if (buffer->memory == V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF) {
 			int fd = rkmpp_buffer->planes[i].fd;
+			/*
+			 * Only ask for the access this direction needs.
+			 * copy_to reads from the MPP buffer and writes here;
+			 * the other way round this mapping is read-only.
+			 *
+			 * It matters because VIDIOC_EXPBUF with flags == 0
+			 * gives a read-only dma-buf - videobuf2 passes
+			 * flags & O_ACCMODE straight through, and O_RDONLY is
+			 * zero - so demanding PROT_WRITE to import a capture
+			 * buffer fails on a caller that did nothing wrong.
+			 * ustreamer exports exactly that way, which is why
+			 * its INPUT-DMA queue never got off the ground here.
+			 */
 			addrs[i] = mmap(NULL, sizes[i],
-					PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
+					copy_to ? (PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE)
+						: PROT_READ,
 					MAP_SHARED, fd, offsets[i]);
 			if (addrs[i] == MAP_FAILED)
 				goto out;
